  "note": "The SHARED golden fixture for the UCT Relative Strength MANSFIELD columns (plan 2026-11-05 §7 item 13; KB 01-methodologies §2; api/services/relative_strength.compute_mansfield_columns, unit 2a-02). 70 hand-designed WEEKLY bars (Friday-dated, t = 1735862400 + i×604800) plus a `benchmarkBars` sibling, exactly as rs_events_default carries its second series; the benchmark has NO bar at the stock's bar 40 (the gap). params.length = 10 is the SMA length (Weinstein's n is 52 weekly / 200 daily; kept short so every window fits on paper). `expected` holds every key of relative_strength.PHASE2A_COLUMNS (5), aligned to `bars`, null for None. FORMULA: RP = (close / benchmark close) × 100; MRS = (RP / SMA(RP, 10) − 1) × 100, the SMA over the VALID bars in order (bar 40 is skipped, never zeroed). mansfield = MRS; null for the first 9 valid bars (warm-up = length − 1) and on the gap bar. mansfieldState = INTS in {-1, 0, 1, null}: 1 above zero AND rising, -1 below zero AND falling, 0 neutral (above but falling, below but rising); null where MRS[t] or MRS[t−1] is null (bars 0-9, 40, 41). mansfieldCrossUp / mansfieldCrossDown = {0.0, 1.0, null}: (MRS[t] ≥ 0) ∧ (MRS[t−1] < 0) and the mirror — the same ≥ rsAbove uses — null where either bar is null. mansfieldCrossBarsAgo = bars since the last zero cross in EITHER direction (the sign of `mansfield` on the same bar says which): 0.0 on the cross bar, counting up by one per bar, and counting THROUGH the gap-adjacent null bars (a hole in the event column is 'no event seen', never a reset); null before the first cross (bars 0-22) and on the gap bar itself. HAND-DERIVED ROWS (where a window is quoted as closes the benchmark is 100 on every bar of it, so RS = close/100 and RP = close): BAR 9 — the first MRS: closes 0..9 sum 509.7, mean 50.97; MRS = (52.0/50.97 − 1) × 100 = 2.020797; state null (no prior MRS), crosses null, age null. BAR 20 — above but FALLING: closes 11..20 sum 560.9, mean 56.09; MRS = (58.4/56.09 − 1) × 100 = 4.118381, below MRS[19] = 5.566565 ⇒ state 0, crossUp 0, crossDown 0, age null (no cross yet). BAR 23 — the first CROSS DOWN: closes 14..23 sum 572.0, mean 57.20; MRS = (57.0/57.20 − 1) × 100 = −0.349650 < 0 while MRS[22] = 0.983491 ≥ 0 ⇒ crossDown 1, crossUp 0, state −1 (below and falling), age 0. BAR 28 — BEAR: closes 19..28 sum 567.3, mean 56.73; MRS = (54.6/56.73 − 1) × 100 = −3.754627, below MRS[27] = −3.434981 ⇒ state −1, age 5. BAR 29 — below but RISING: closes 20..29 sum 562.9, mean 56.29; MRS = (54.2/56.29 − 1) × 100 = −3.712915, above MRS[28] ⇒ state 0, age 6. BAR 41 — the bar after the GAP, the SMA skips bar 40: RP over bars 31..39 and 41 = 100 × (53.8/101.5, 53.9/102, 53.6/102.5, 53.7/103, 53.5/103.5, 53.6/104, 53.8/104.5, 54.2/105, 54.6/105.5, 54.3/106) = 53.004926, 52.843137, 52.292683, 52.135922, 51.690821, 51.538462, 51.483254, 51.619048, 51.753555, 51.226415; mean 51.958822; MRS = (51.226415/51.958822 − 1) × 100 = −1.409591; state and both crosses null (MRS[40] is null); age 18 = 41 − 23, counted through the gap. BAR 43 — the CROSS UP: RP over bars 33..39, 41, 42, 43 = 52.292683, 52.135922, 51.690821, 51.538462, 51.483254, 51.619048, 51.753555, 51.226415, 51.603774, 52.511848; mean 51.785578; MRS = (52.511848/51.785578 − 1) × 100 = 1.402457 ≥ 0 while MRS[42] = −0.414780 < 0 ⇒ crossUp 1, crossDown 0, state 1 (above and rising), age 0. BAR 64 — below but rising after the second cross down (bar 62): closes 55..64 sum 629.6, mean 62.96; MRS = (62.5/62.96 − 1) × 100 = −0.730623, above MRS[63] = −0.968100 ⇒ state 0, age 2. CROSSES BY INDEX: crossDown at [23, 62], crossUp at [43]. The benchmark is NOT constant (bars 30-39 and 41-53 vary), so a Mansfield computed from the stock's close alone cannot satisfy this file. Written by a one-off script that asserted every claim above before writing anything; `_generate.py` was not run (regeneration is banned — _schema.md). 2026-11-07 (visual round VA1, spec A2): dotMansfieldCross carries crosses UP only, at 0.0 on the zero line; it was the Mansfield value at either cross.",
